Not quite.  Each level of rust/corrosion/burning takes away one point of 
AC up to the base AC of an item.  Enchantments do not matter as far as 
this goes.  I've usually been ignoring fooproofing most types of armor in 
a lot of my games lately since it tends to have little effect overall.  
Early game you should consider blessing a ?oEA and using it to try to get 
more than one point of ac rather than using it to proof and repair armor.  
Exceptions for armors that grant more than one ac that you plan to keep.  
Robe or cloak of protection come to mind, unless you plan to stick with a 
dwarven iron helm thru the whole game.

You could get a nice burnt up +5 t-shirt and you would still get +5 ac 
from it.

